			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Fire $acceptModelSaved after disk writes; strip Undo/Redo from native Edit menu\n\n**T1.4 save notification** — `FileWriteNative` and `TextfileWrite` now fire `$acceptModelSaved` via Vine after a successful disk write, so Cocoon can dispatch `onDidSaveTextDocument` to subscribed extensions (format-on-save, organize-imports, save listeners). The save is fire-and-forget (tokio::spawn) so a Vine failure never cascades back to the workbench IPC caller. Both handlers also gain `dev_log` instrumentation for write latency and byte count.\n\n**Cmd+Z routing fix** — On macOS, Tauri's default `Builder::default()` installs an Edit submenu with native Undo/Redo items that intercept Cmd+Z at the AppKit responder-chain level before the WKWebView's keydown handler fires, preventing VS Code's Monaco editor from seeing `meta+z`. The new `AppMenu::SetAppMenu` builds a custom Edit submenu containing only Cut/Copy/Paste/SelectAll, removing Undo/Redo so Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z reach the JS layer. Called from `AppLifecycleSetup` immediately after window creation. Non-fatal; logs a warning and keeps the default menu if the override fails. No-op on Windows/Linux.",
			"SHA": "f79990166465444bbe3a00ca968af7527b0bea13"
		},
